<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕnē^brĭcōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		tenebricus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of darkness</i> or <i>gloom</i>,
				<i>shrouded in darkness</i>, <i>dark</i>, <i>gloomy</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">esse sensus non obscuros sed tenebricosos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 23, 73</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">popina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Pis. 8, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libidines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Prov. Cons. 4, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenebricosissimum tempus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Vatin. 5, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 3,
					11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus angustus et tenebricosus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 9, 19</span></i>
			.</div>
